 ## 2. Corrections — these were in the original spec, dropped or wrongly generalized in the last build, put back exactly as stated

 - **Revenue widget**: a real, literal Home-grid widget (not a generic "custom metric" placeholder) — $ total over last 30 days, % change, paid-customer count. Tap the tile to open a detail view. Requires the user to configure a Stripe endpoint/API key in Settings to power it.
 - **Visitors widget**: a real, literal widget — live count, % change, 30-day sparkline. This one is **not part of the default Home grid** — it should only appear as an option inside the "+ Add Widget" picker, and only show up on the Home grid after the user explicitly adds it.
 - **Claude usage widget**: a real, literal widget — token count, day streak, weekly bar chart. Restore as its own named widget, not folded into anything generic.
 - **Drink Water widget**: fully missing from the last build — on/off nudge toggle, tally of glasses (with an add button), adjustable reminder interval. Belongs with the Time tab group (alongside Pomodoro/Timer/Stopwatch/Alarms) or Home — your call on placement, but it must exist.
 - **Quick timer widget** (Home grid version): confirm this uses the circular-dial aesthetic from the original design (matching the Pomodoro/System-stats ring style), not a plain numeric countdown.
 - **Files/converter tab** — restore full detail, not just "image/file converter": JPEG/PNG/HEIC/PDF conversion targets, a quality slider, max-size presets (1024px / 1920px / 2560px / original), and a batch queue showing a "done" output list with share/preview actions per converted file.
 - **Clipboard tab** — restore full detail: word/char count per item, source app, timestamp, and individual pin/delete controls per clipboard entry (not just "a snippet store" with no UI specifics).
 - **Tab dock chrome** — restore explicitly: the bottom row of tab icons must be user-reorderable (drag to rearrange), and there must be a visible "+" button to add a new tab (surfacing the config-driven custom-tab picker from the original spec).

 ## 3. New additions (this follow-up)

 - **Clipboard tab — add a to-do list / kanban-style panel** alongside the clipboard history, within the same tab (e.g. a secondary sub-view or side panel, your call on layout) — simple task list or lightweight kanban columns, local storage only.
 - **Notification/pop-in animation** — any transient notification (a "copied," "conversion finished," "backup finished" style pop-in — the Tier-2 "transient" category from the arbitration rule in the original prompt) should render as a highlight that **slides right-to-left across the notch display**, not a plain fade-in-place. Apply this consistently to every transient pop-in, not per-feature custom animations.
 - **Daily word learner** — a small feature/widget that surfaces one new word per day with its meaning and a simple example sentence. Language is user-configurable — support multiple target languages and let the user pick which one(s) they want words in. Decide whether this lives on Home as a small widget or as its own tab; either is fine, but it must be there.
 - **Fix: Home-grid tiles must be draggable/reorderable.** This was specified in the original "Edit widgets" mode and either wasn't implemented or is broken in the current build — user cannot currently drag tiles to reorder them. Implement proper drag-and-drop reordering (e.g. SwiftUI `onDrag`/`onDrop`, or a dedicated reorder-mode with drag handles) with the resulting order persisted, not reset on relaunch.
 - **Calendar — real Google Calendar integration**, not just relying on Apple's Calendar app/EventKit. Add an OAuth-based Google Calendar API connection so the user can link their Google account directly, as an addition or alternative to the existing Apple Calendar (EventKit) source — don't assume the user has already added Google as a macOS system calendar account.
 - **Calendar — add a mini full-month view**: a proper month grid (day cells, event indicator dots), not only the "up next" agenda-style list from the original spec. Both should be available in the tab — agenda view for the immediate glance, month view for a wider look.

